    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0336" n="218" xml:id="pg218"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/9814: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-03-19T19:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 19,
                                1928—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 19—2:45 p.m.<anchor
                            n="35" xml:id="d150-f1"/>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>174. My 160, March 13, 4 p.m.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d150-f2"/></p>
                <p>1. Following is summary of mail despatch from American consul general [at]
                    Tientsin under date of March 13th; copies of which are going forward to
                    Department in next pouch:</p>
                <p>[Here follows a summary of the despatch, printed <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>2. I concur in Gauss statement of probabilities of situation and recommendation
                    for protection of Americans at Peitaiho.</p>
                <p>3. Repeated to commander in chief for information North China Patrol.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
